{
  "about": "The transit systems the transit ride types use (core.transit), each from its own static GTFS, fetched and compacted on the host (scripts/fetch_transit_gtfs.py, scripts/build_transit_schedule.py; docs/OPERATIONS.md). The feeds and the file built from them are never committed (docs/SOURCES.md). `bike.vehicle`: all = every trip takes a bike; trip = only trips with GTFS bikes_allowed 1; offpeak = every trip outside weekday rush (06:00-09:30, 15:00-19:00); none = no bike (unclear bike access is closed). `bike.station`: elevator = the map's Metro elevators (WMATA); station = every station of the system (the owner, 2026-10-12: \"I believe all stations have ways to board with either ramps or elevators. Most people can carry bikes up and down stairs in a pinch.\"); any = a bus stop at the curb. `words` names a vehicle in a step: {route} is the route's name. `route_name`: long = a route is named by GTFS route_long_name first (\"Fredericksburg Line\", not VRE's short name \"2\"). `idle_notes`: say plainly when a route near the trip has no service at that time.",
  "systems": [
    {
      "id": "wmata-rail",
      "name": "Metro",
      "operator": "WMATA",
      "mode": "metro",
      "stations": "wmata-map",
      "words": "the {route}",
      "idle_notes": true,
      "feed": {
        "file": "wmata-rail-gtfs.zip",
        "url": "https://api.wmata.com/gtfs/rail-gtfs-static.zip",
        "key_env": "WMATA_API_KEY",
        "key_header": "api_key"
      },
      "bike": {
        "vehicle": "all",
        "station": "elevator",
        "rule": "Use the elevators and a car's end doors.",
        "source": "https://www.wmata.com/ride/guides/bikes/bikes-on-rail.html"
      },
      "credit": "WMATA GTFS (scheduled times)"
    },
    {
      "id": "wmata-bus",
      "name": "Metrobus",
      "operator": "WMATA",
      "mode": "bus",
      "words": "bus {route}",
      "idle_notes": false,
      "feed": {
        "file": "wmata-bus-gtfs.zip",
        "url": "https://api.wmata.com/gtfs/bus-gtfs-static.zip",
        "key_env": "WMATA_API_KEY",
        "key_header": "api_key"
      },
      "bike": {
        "vehicle": "all",
        "station": "any",
        "rule": "Use the front bike rack.",
        "source": "https://www.wmata.com/ride/guides/bikes/bikes-on-bus.html"
      },
      "credit": "WMATA GTFS (scheduled times)"
    },
    {
